 "response": "Driril's budget is now **$1528K**. I worked this out by hand from the records, with no tool or independent re-check, so a slip in the long running sum is possible.\n\n**How I got there**\n\n1. Only Finance Office records change the budget. Every Sales, PMO, Vendor, Legal, Operations, Marketing, Engineering and Facilities message was ignored.\n2. The starting point is #0001, which sets the budget to $1630K. No later Finance Office record sets an absolute value, so every other update is an increase or a decrease.\n3. I resolved each chain of withdrawals from the end backwards. A withdrawal only counts if it has not itself been withdrawn. Some examples:\n   - **#0004 counts.** #0019 withdrew it, but #0114 withdrew #0019.\n   - **#0024 counts.** #0566 voids #0116, so #0047 stands. #0047 voids #0032, so #0024 is restored.\n   - **#0014 does not count.** #0532 voids #0286, so #0035 stands and withdraws #0014.\n   - **#0473 does not count.** #1039 voids #0924, so #0720 stands. #0720 voids #0631, so #0571 stands and withdraws #0473.\n   - **#0214 counts.** #1596 voids #1006, so #0254 stands. #0254 voids #0225, so #0214 is restored.\n   - **#0064 counts.** #1231 voids #0381, so #0184 stands. #0184 voids #0168, so #0064 is restored.\n4. I then applied every increase and decrease that remained effective, once each, in record order from $1630K through #1600.\n\nANSWER: $1528K",
